From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam <i@noc.cat>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:53:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 80/80] net: stmmac: tc956x: give the RX queue the whole RX FIFO

The driver split 32KiB of the 46KiB RX FIFO evenly over four RX queues.
Nothing steers received frames across those queues, so every frame
lands in queue 0 and has 8KiB of FIFO, which fills in about 26us at
2.5Gb/s. The RX DMA does not drain line-rate bursts that fast. On the
Radxa Dragon Q8B a single iperf3 TCP stream into the port overflowed
the FIFO about ten thousand times in ten seconds; the PAUSE frames sent
meanwhile did not prevent it, and TCP backed off to under 100Mbit/s.
Four parallel streams reached 270Mbit/s.

Use one RX queue and give it the whole RX FIFO. A single stream now
reaches 2.25Gbit/s and four streams 2.31Gbit/s, with a handful of
overflows across millions of frames. Transmit, which keeps its four
queues of 8KiB, is unchanged at 2.2Gbit/s.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
index ed01ba2..f7694d7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-tc956x.c
@@ -642,11 +642,12 @@ static int tc956x_plat_dat_init(struct tc956x_data *td)
 	plat->unicast_filter_entries = 32;
 
 	/*
-	 * TC956x has 8 RX queues but we observe significantly reduced RX
-	 * bandwidth if we don't have at least 8k FIFO space per queue, so
-	 * by default we avoid using all the queues.
+	 * TC956x has 8 RX queues, but nothing steers received frames across
+	 * them: every frame lands in queue 0. Use that one queue and give it
+	 * the whole RX FIFO. A queue with 8KiB overflows on line-rate bursts
+	 * at 2.5G, and TCP then backs off to a fraction of the link speed.
 	 */
-	plat->rx_queues_to_use = 4;
+	plat->rx_queues_to_use = 1;
 
 	/*
 	 * TC956x has 8 TX queues but only #0 to #3 work for general IP traffic.
@@ -655,13 +656,12 @@ static int tc956x_plat_dat_init(struct tc956x_data *td)
 	plat->tx_queues_to_use = 4;
 
 	/*
-	 * Oversized FIFOs result in reduced performance in bandwidth tests.
+	 * Oversized TX FIFOs result in reduced performance in bandwidth tests.
 	 * Limit them to 8KiB per queue, or the total available.
 	 */
 	plat->tx_fifo_size =
 		min(TC956X_TX_FIFO_KB, 8 * plat->tx_queues_to_use) * SZ_1K;
-	plat->rx_fifo_size =
-		min(TC956X_RX_FIFO_KB, 8 * plat->rx_queues_to_use) * SZ_1K;
+	plat->rx_fifo_size = TC956X_RX_FIFO_KB * SZ_1K;
 	plat->host_dma_width = 36;
 
 	plat->rx_sched_algorithm = MTL_RX_ALGORITHM_SP;
